<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06GW">Example <span data-tag="06GW">9.4.1.3</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ denote the $\infty $-category of (small) $\infty $-categories (Construction <a data-tag="0209" href="/tag/0209">5.5.3.1</a>). Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ is compactly generated. It admits small colimits (Corollary <a data-tag="02V1" href="/tag/02V1">7.4.5.3</a>), and every object $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\in \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ can be realized as a small filtered colimits of essentially finite $\infty $-categories (Proposition <a data-tag="06FV" href="/tag/06FV">9.3.2.24</a>), which are compact by virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="068G" href="/tag/068G">9.2.7.9</a>. </p>
